1
00:00:23,771 --> 00:00:26,980
I knew it. That dress looks best on you.

2
00:00:30,938 --> 00:00:32,771
Don't you agree, Ichito?

3
00:00:33,813 --> 00:00:36,480
Your mother looks beautiful in white.

4
00:02:05,105 --> 00:02:08,313
She's been like this
for several years now.

5
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,646
The chances of her regaining consciousness

6
00:02:17,063 --> 00:02:18,521
are low, aren't they?

7
00:02:19,396 --> 00:02:20,396
Yes.

8
00:02:21,896 --> 00:02:24,146
As I explained earlier,

9
00:02:24,230 --> 00:02:26,313
her brain was deprived of blood flow,

10
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:28,771
causing severe damage.

11
00:02:29,271 --> 00:02:31,480
I'm afraid the chances are slim.

12
00:02:33,855 --> 00:02:36,355
If anything comes up,
please press the call button.

13
00:02:55,646 --> 00:02:56,855
I should've…

14
00:02:59,313 --> 00:03:01,605
come to see her sooner.

15
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:06,396
It's not your fault.

16
00:03:21,646 --> 00:03:23,313
Professor Toyohara.

17
00:03:31,771 --> 00:03:34,313
I never thought you'd come here.

18
00:03:36,563 --> 00:03:37,896
I let my guard down.

19
00:03:40,230 --> 00:03:42,063
Why are you here?

20
00:03:45,855 --> 00:03:49,771
Your father and I
were close friends in college.

21
00:03:51,896 --> 00:03:54,146
We eventually drifted apart though.

22
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:58,396
I even changed your diapers
when you were a baby.

23
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:03,938
After the incident,

24
00:04:04,730 --> 00:04:08,021
I'd come to check on
Sanae from time to time.

25
00:04:10,146 --> 00:04:14,438
Why did you keep quiet all this time?

26
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:19,480
Because I knew
you were avoiding your mother.

27
00:04:21,313 --> 00:04:23,855
I thought having someone nearby
who knew your past

28
00:04:24,355 --> 00:04:26,271
would only hurt you.

29
00:04:29,813 --> 00:04:32,021
All this time, I've been so hard on you.

30
00:04:32,730 --> 00:04:33,813
I'm sorry.

31
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:38,230
I'd selfishly hoped

32
00:04:38,313 --> 00:04:44,021
you'd leave the past behind
and choose a path other than sex therapy.

33
00:04:53,146 --> 00:04:54,396
<i>It was as if</i>

34
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:58,188
<i>time had stopped.</i>

35
00:05:01,896 --> 00:05:05,646
<i>My mother as I remembered her</i>
<i>is still there…</i>

36
00:05:08,063 --> 00:05:09,730
<i>in that room.</i>

37
00:05:11,938 --> 00:05:13,438
Sanae

38
00:05:14,813 --> 00:05:17,105
doesn't remember the incident.

39
00:05:19,730 --> 00:05:20,646
What?

40
00:05:21,396 --> 00:05:23,188
It's likely a dissociative disorder.

41
00:05:24,188 --> 00:05:26,230
Her time has been frozen

42
00:05:26,896 --> 00:05:28,896
since before the incident.

43
00:05:32,188 --> 00:05:33,896
Even when she was conscious,

44
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:37,938
she always talked about
the day your voice changed,

45
00:05:38,855 --> 00:05:41,730
or when you made her <i>omurice</i>
for Mother's Day.

46
00:05:47,896 --> 00:05:49,313
Professor.

47
00:05:50,605 --> 00:05:52,438
Do you know…

48
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:56,105
why…

49
00:05:58,105 --> 00:06:00,146
that incident happened?

50
00:06:02,730 --> 00:06:04,271
I don't.

51
00:06:08,021 --> 00:06:09,021
But…

52
00:06:11,855 --> 00:06:15,938
I did catch glimpses
of the pressure she was under.

53
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:19,396
Pressure?

54
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:26,938
Your father was a brilliant surgeon.

55
00:06:28,771 --> 00:06:31,396
You could say he's an idealist to a fault.

56
00:06:33,896 --> 00:06:35,771
Those ideals…

57
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:40,396
were also imposed on Sanae.

58
00:06:42,813 --> 00:06:44,646
He appeared to be molding her

59
00:06:46,355 --> 00:06:48,605
into a beautiful wife…

60
00:06:50,855 --> 00:06:54,438
and the ideal mother.

61
00:06:55,813 --> 00:06:57,021
Everything from

62
00:06:58,021 --> 00:06:59,646
the clothes she wore

63
00:07:00,271 --> 00:07:01,688
to her hairstyle.

64
00:07:04,563 --> 00:07:07,771
I knew it. That dress looks best on you.

65
00:07:10,271 --> 00:07:13,938
That pressure drove her to the brink.

66
00:07:15,605 --> 00:07:19,063
She likely turned to an affair
as a way to escape.

67
00:07:21,313 --> 00:07:23,980
Your father couldn't forgive that.

68
00:07:25,396 --> 00:07:28,021
His anger wasn't aimed at Sanae,
who was like a doll,

69
00:07:29,271 --> 00:07:31,605
but at the man…

70
00:07:33,771 --> 00:07:35,855
who stole that doll from him.

71
00:07:42,730 --> 00:07:43,980
My father

72
00:07:44,896 --> 00:07:48,896
probably had a Pygmalion complex.

73
00:07:51,396 --> 00:07:54,855
Pygmalion complex?

74
00:07:57,105 --> 00:07:58,646
In the narrow sense,

75
00:07:59,188 --> 00:08:00,896
it's an obsession with dolls.

76
00:08:02,438 --> 00:08:04,938
But more broadly,

77
00:08:05,438 --> 00:08:10,813
it's the desire to shape someone
into your ideal and control them.

78
00:08:16,771 --> 00:08:17,938
All this time,

79
00:08:18,771 --> 00:08:22,396
I thought my mother was the one
with a sexual problem.

80
00:08:24,688 --> 00:08:25,688
But…

81
00:08:26,896 --> 00:08:29,521
the one who had a problem

82
00:08:30,521 --> 00:08:32,188
was my father.

83
00:08:35,271 --> 00:08:38,313
CTN CENTRAL TELEVISION

84
00:08:38,396 --> 00:08:42,980
<i>These stairs have 40 steps going up,</i>
<i>but only 39 coming down.</i>

85
00:08:43,063 --> 00:08:45,855
<i>The mysterious stairway</i>
<i>known as the "Ghost Stairs."</i>

86
00:08:46,563 --> 00:08:48,438
<i>When you walk down them,</i>

87
00:08:48,521 --> 00:08:52,688
<i>the last step is very slightly tilted.</i>

88
00:08:53,355 --> 00:08:57,188
The part where you say,
"The last step is very slightly tilted,"

89
00:08:57,271 --> 00:09:00,771
could you do it again
with a slightly more reflective tone?

90
00:09:03,355 --> 00:09:04,563
Ms. Ichinose?

91
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:07,563
Yes?

92
00:09:07,646 --> 00:09:09,480
Are you okay? Need a break?

93
00:09:09,563 --> 00:09:11,063
Sorry. I'm fine.

94
00:09:16,521 --> 00:09:18,188
Morning, Ichinose.

95
00:09:18,271 --> 00:09:19,563
Got a minute?

96
00:09:23,105 --> 00:09:25,146
"Women Leading the Future" Week?

97
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:29,771
The higher-ups came up
with the concept to modernize

98
00:09:29,855 --> 00:09:32,271
the network's old-fashioned image.

99
00:09:33,355 --> 00:09:36,688
They say it's going to be
a weeklong, network-wide special.

100
00:09:36,771 --> 00:09:39,230
And our show got roped into it too.

101
00:09:45,188 --> 00:09:48,105
As you can see,
nothing's really set in stone yet.

102
00:09:48,188 --> 00:09:51,605
Can you and Mitarai
brainstorm a few ideas?

103
00:09:52,396 --> 00:09:53,396
Huh?

104
00:09:55,605 --> 00:09:56,896
Are you sure?

105
00:09:56,980 --> 00:09:58,188
Can I really do it?

106
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:00,480
Why else would I be asking you?

107
00:10:01,105 --> 00:10:02,105
I'll leave it to you.

108
00:10:02,855 --> 00:10:04,146
Oh, um…

109
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:06,813
Why me?

110
00:10:07,313 --> 00:10:08,313
Well…

111
00:10:08,938 --> 00:10:11,355
Someone said you'd be perfect for it.

112
00:10:11,855 --> 00:10:12,980
I'm counting on you.

113
00:10:15,230 --> 00:10:17,688
Oh? Long time no see.

114
00:10:22,813 --> 00:10:24,021
Mr. Kazuma.

115
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:25,980
Hey.

116
00:10:26,563 --> 00:10:28,563
Was it you who recommended me

117
00:10:28,646 --> 00:10:30,230
for the project?

118
00:10:30,730 --> 00:10:31,730
Huh?

119
00:10:33,313 --> 00:10:35,230
"Women Leading the Future" Week.

120
00:10:35,730 --> 00:10:38,271
Oh. You're part of it too, Ichinose?

121
00:10:39,188 --> 00:10:41,063
Uh… Yes.

122
00:10:41,563 --> 00:10:42,605
Good for you.

123
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:49,355
If you need anything,
come talk to me anytime.

124
00:11:20,396 --> 00:11:24,730
I really meant it when I asked you
why you chose to work in sex therapy.

125
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:28,605
Was this career

126
00:11:30,438 --> 00:11:33,771
a path you actually chose for yourself?

127
00:11:38,396 --> 00:11:39,730
Doctor.

128
00:11:39,813 --> 00:11:41,605
Do you have a minute?

129
00:11:41,688 --> 00:11:43,480
It's a real mess over there.

130
00:11:43,563 --> 00:11:45,230
Could you come over?

131
00:11:45,313 --> 00:11:46,313
Sorry.

132
00:11:48,230 --> 00:11:49,313
Look.

133
00:11:51,730 --> 00:11:54,896
Whoa. What's going on here?

134
00:11:54,980 --> 00:11:56,771
I thought I'd make some dried herbs

135
00:11:56,855 --> 00:11:58,938
since we don't have
any appointments right now.

136
00:12:00,230 --> 00:12:03,105
Could you bundle these up?
Three or four stems each.

137
00:12:03,188 --> 00:12:04,605
Huh? Uh, sure.

138
00:12:04,688 --> 00:12:07,396
As for you, Saikawa…

139
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:08,480
What?

140
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:11,063
Here.

141
00:12:11,563 --> 00:12:12,563
Huh?

142
00:12:22,938 --> 00:12:24,230
They smell nice.

143
00:12:24,313 --> 00:12:25,230
They do.

144
00:12:25,730 --> 00:12:28,646
Herbs retain their fragrance
even after they've been cut.

145
00:12:28,730 --> 00:12:30,021
A bug!

146
00:12:30,521 --> 00:12:33,355
Fresh herbs have
a refreshing, youthful scent.

147
00:12:33,438 --> 00:12:36,813
Once dried, their scent becomes
more mellow and concentrated.

148
00:12:36,896 --> 00:12:39,313
-Whoa! A bug!
-You're so loud!

149
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:44,313
Keep it down a little, will you?

150
00:12:47,146 --> 00:12:48,146
Okay.

151
00:12:50,396 --> 00:12:52,021
No matter what form they take,

152
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:55,521
the fragrance of a flower
that once bloomed always lingers.

153
00:13:07,896 --> 00:13:09,271
Excuse me.

154
00:13:18,938 --> 00:13:21,438
Um, I don't have an appointment.

155
00:13:21,521 --> 00:13:22,480
Is that okay?

156
00:13:22,563 --> 00:13:24,021
Oh, yes.

157
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,396
I…

158
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:39,146
attended one of your lectures
at the university.

159
00:13:48,146 --> 00:13:49,771
Ms. Yuka Namioka.

160
00:13:51,021 --> 00:13:52,021
Yes.

161
00:13:53,605 --> 00:13:55,771
What brings you in today?

162
00:13:57,480 --> 00:13:59,438
I guess it's a concern.

163
00:14:00,355 --> 00:14:04,021
Maybe it's not even something
I should be worrying about.

164
00:14:06,938 --> 00:14:09,313
If it's troubling you,

165
00:14:09,396 --> 00:14:11,021
then it's a concern.

166
00:14:19,771 --> 00:14:23,646
One of my professors at the university

167
00:14:24,605 --> 00:14:27,605
started looking at me in a sexual way.

168
00:14:28,813 --> 00:14:31,021
I might just be imagining it.

169
00:14:32,896 --> 00:14:36,063
If you don't mind sharing,
could you tell me what happened?

170
00:14:38,771 --> 00:14:41,146
I'm an undergrad student.

171
00:14:41,646 --> 00:14:45,855
I started spending more time in a lab
where I wanted to pursue my research.

172
00:14:46,646 --> 00:14:49,105
The professor was easy to talk to,

173
00:14:49,855 --> 00:14:53,896
and he was supportive of my research too.

174
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:56,105
He started looking out for me.

175
00:14:57,355 --> 00:14:59,271
It might sound like I'm bragging,

176
00:14:59,355 --> 00:15:01,063
but that's not what I mean.

177
00:15:04,938 --> 00:15:08,938
He started inviting me
to the lab's social gatherings too.

178
00:15:09,021 --> 00:15:11,730
At first, I was happy.

179
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:17,271
But eventually, he'd start asking me
to lunch one-on-one

180
00:15:18,063 --> 00:15:22,396
and only take me to overnight conferences.

181
00:15:23,605 --> 00:15:25,980
It's not like he ever touched me

182
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:30,063
or tried to share a hotel room with me.

183
00:15:31,230 --> 00:15:34,730
That's why I couldn't tell anyone.

184
00:15:35,730 --> 00:15:38,980
You started feeling like
he was looking at you sexually,

185
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:40,813
and that made you uncomfortable?

186
00:15:45,563 --> 00:15:47,230
Even at conferences,

187
00:15:47,730 --> 00:15:50,313
he always kept me at his side.

188
00:15:51,646 --> 00:15:54,063
It felt less like
a professor and a student,

189
00:15:54,146 --> 00:15:56,271
and more like I was his poster girl.

190
00:15:57,021 --> 00:15:59,646
He even bought me clothes
to wear to the conferences.

191
00:16:03,813 --> 00:16:06,313
He'd often invite me out for dessert,

192
00:16:06,396 --> 00:16:09,146
saying it was awkward
for an older man to go alone.

193
00:16:10,605 --> 00:16:12,438
He likes sweets after all.

194
00:16:13,563 --> 00:16:14,855
Professor Kurusu.

195
00:16:24,771 --> 00:16:26,105
How's this?

196
00:16:31,605 --> 00:16:32,896
Think it'll get approved?

197
00:16:32,980 --> 00:16:33,813
Hard to say.

198
00:16:33,896 --> 00:16:36,646
It doesn't have
the kind of hook Mr. Kujo likes.

199
00:16:36,730 --> 00:16:39,855
Yeah. You're right.

200
00:16:39,938 --> 00:16:42,480
Sorry for keeping you so late.

201
00:16:42,563 --> 00:16:45,396
Not at all. I really think
it's a good concept.

202
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:49,313
So maybe you should try applying
your own style of journalism.

203
00:16:50,355 --> 00:16:51,855
Back when we were trainees,

204
00:16:51,938 --> 00:16:54,313
I thought you could even
make it as a journalist.

205
00:16:56,521 --> 00:16:57,646
Thanks.

206
00:16:58,855 --> 00:17:01,896
Thank you. I'm so lucky
to have a coworker like you!

207
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:07,521
By the way, were you the one
who recommended me for the project?

208
00:17:08,021 --> 00:17:09,521
Thank you so much.

209
00:17:09,605 --> 00:17:11,521
No. That wasn't me.

210
00:17:12,105 --> 00:17:12,938
Huh?

211
00:17:14,063 --> 00:17:14,896
What?

212
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:15,813
Huh?

213
00:17:17,188 --> 00:17:19,605
This proposal focuses on
Japan's lagging sex education

214
00:17:19,688 --> 00:17:23,480
and low awareness of sexuality.

215
00:17:26,605 --> 00:17:28,313
It still feels a bit too serious.

216
00:17:30,813 --> 00:17:32,146
I'm fine with the concept,

217
00:17:32,230 --> 00:17:34,730
but it needs a stronger hook.

218
00:17:34,813 --> 00:17:35,813
Right.

219
00:17:37,771 --> 00:17:41,146
Japan ranks low on the Gender Gap Index.

220
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:43,730
Among its categories,
"Political Empowerment"--

221
00:17:43,813 --> 00:17:45,688
Again, that's the kind of story

222
00:17:45,771 --> 00:17:48,105
News One runs during the ten o'clock hour.

223
00:17:48,188 --> 00:17:49,896
We're an evening news show.

224
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:52,146
We need to make it more engaging.

225
00:17:52,230 --> 00:17:53,521
-Right.
-Harashima!

226
00:17:53,605 --> 00:17:54,730
-Sorry.
-Okay.

227
00:17:54,813 --> 00:17:55,730
Um…

228
00:17:55,813 --> 00:17:59,188
Do you all know what
the Pygmalion complex is?

229
00:18:00,521 --> 00:18:01,355
Pyg…

230
00:18:02,188 --> 00:18:04,021
I only learned about it recently.

231
00:18:04,646 --> 00:18:10,521
It's when people, especially men,
treat women like dolls

232
00:18:10,605 --> 00:18:13,480
and force their ideals onto them.

233
00:18:17,521 --> 00:18:19,521
I feel like up until now,

234
00:18:20,021 --> 00:18:24,855
I've been living up to the ideal image
the company and viewers expect of me.

235
00:18:25,438 --> 00:18:28,980
But I don't think that's just because
I'm a female announcer.

236
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:31,313
I think it's a sense of discomfort

237
00:18:31,396 --> 00:18:34,230
many women in this country feel
to some extent.

238
00:18:36,230 --> 00:18:40,230
People impose their ideal
of womanhood onto us

239
00:18:40,313 --> 00:18:43,230
and silence us like we're dolls.

240
00:18:43,896 --> 00:18:45,938
And sex is a classic example of--

241
00:18:46,021 --> 00:18:47,188
Ichinose.

242
00:18:47,271 --> 00:18:48,896
It's still serious.

243
00:18:49,396 --> 00:18:50,438
Too serious.

244
00:18:52,063 --> 00:18:53,480
Well…

245
00:18:55,813 --> 00:18:57,271
Basically,

246
00:18:57,771 --> 00:19:01,646
women should talk openly
about sex too, right?

247
00:19:03,146 --> 00:19:03,980
Right.

248
00:19:04,563 --> 00:19:05,646
Exactly.

249
00:19:05,730 --> 00:19:06,813
That's it.

250
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:08,855
So I want to use this opportunity

251
00:19:08,938 --> 00:19:12,938
to cover the topic of sex head-on.

252
00:19:14,105 --> 00:19:16,105
Wow. That's pretty direct.

253
00:19:17,146 --> 00:19:20,563
A female announcer
doing a feature like that

254
00:19:20,646 --> 00:19:22,271
would definitely draw attention.

255
00:19:23,146 --> 00:19:26,646
We can use people's nosy curiosity
to our advantage.

256
00:19:26,730 --> 00:19:28,146
Right, Mr. Kujo?

257
00:19:28,938 --> 00:19:30,688
All right. We'll give it a try.

258
00:19:31,313 --> 00:19:32,313
Let's do it.

259
00:19:33,063 --> 00:19:34,271
What about the title?

260
00:19:36,521 --> 00:19:37,355
Anyone?

261
00:19:38,271 --> 00:19:41,188
What about "Sex Problems
You Can't Tell Anyone About"?

262
00:19:42,605 --> 00:19:43,605
That's good.

263
00:19:43,688 --> 00:19:44,813
I like that.

264
00:19:44,896 --> 00:19:47,646
Mitarai, work with Ichinose
and develop that idea.

265
00:19:47,730 --> 00:19:48,646
Got it.

266
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:50,688
I'll run it by Programming.

267
00:19:50,771 --> 00:19:52,271
I'm counting on you all.

268
00:19:52,355 --> 00:19:53,355
-Okay.
-Thank you.

269
00:19:53,438 --> 00:19:56,146
-Good work, everyone.
-Good work.

270
00:20:19,021 --> 00:20:21,438
The one who brought me onto this project…

271
00:20:22,105 --> 00:20:23,688
Was it you, Miku?

272
00:20:30,521 --> 00:20:31,646
Thank you.

273
00:20:33,355 --> 00:20:34,563
It's nothing.

274
00:20:34,646 --> 00:20:37,063
I just want to make my show better.

275
00:20:41,105 --> 00:20:42,938
Do you remember that time

276
00:20:43,438 --> 00:20:46,563
we were asked to entertain
a sponsor together?

277
00:20:46,646 --> 00:20:47,813
Huh?

278
00:20:48,396 --> 00:20:50,355
One of the clients got drunk

279
00:20:50,438 --> 00:20:53,063
and started sexually harassing us
at the after-party.

280
00:20:54,563 --> 00:20:55,980
Oh, yeah.

281
00:20:56,521 --> 00:21:01,105
You subtly redirected his harassment
toward yourself, didn't you?

282
00:21:01,730 --> 00:21:03,980
So I wouldn't become the target.

283
00:21:07,021 --> 00:21:08,771
I guess I did.

284
00:21:13,605 --> 00:21:17,063
That really pissed me off.

285
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:18,896
Huh?

286
00:21:19,396 --> 00:21:21,730
I wanted you to speak up.

287
00:21:21,813 --> 00:21:24,521
I didn't want to see you
getting hurt to protect me.

288
00:21:24,605 --> 00:21:26,271
I wanted you to call him out.

289
00:21:28,188 --> 00:21:29,313
That's not all.

290
00:21:29,396 --> 00:21:32,438
Female announcers should be free
to date whoever they want.

291
00:21:32,521 --> 00:21:35,063
Why should a scandal
involving your boyfriend's parents

292
00:21:35,146 --> 00:21:37,521
affect your professional reputation?

293
00:21:37,605 --> 00:21:40,063
It disappoints me to see you
put up with it all

294
00:21:40,146 --> 00:21:41,771
and act like a model student!

295
00:21:47,271 --> 00:21:48,105
What?

296
00:21:48,605 --> 00:21:50,188
Did you just laugh?

297
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:52,521
Sorry.

298
00:21:58,313 --> 00:21:59,313
Hey.

299
00:22:00,021 --> 00:22:01,605
Let's grab lunch sometime.

300
00:22:01,688 --> 00:22:04,271
Don't act friendly all of a sudden.

301
00:22:04,355 --> 00:22:06,271
Why not? Let's go.

302
00:22:06,355 --> 00:22:07,896
Come on. What do you like?

303
00:22:09,646 --> 00:22:10,480
Excuse me.

304
00:22:10,563 --> 00:22:14,605
We're asking people around town
about any concerns related to sex.

305
00:22:14,688 --> 00:22:17,646
I'm looking for someone on dating apps.

306
00:22:17,730 --> 00:22:18,605
Excuse me.

307
00:22:18,688 --> 00:22:21,063
This might be hard to say,
but does that mean…

308
00:22:21,146 --> 00:22:22,896
Regarding sexual concerns--

309
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:25,563
You're really asking us that?
That's embarrassing!

310
00:22:26,396 --> 00:22:30,355
Honestly, I thought no one
would want to talk to us,

311
00:22:30,438 --> 00:22:33,521
but a lot more people
shared their concerns than I expected.

312
00:22:34,771 --> 00:22:36,730
I'm kind of in a sexless marriage too.

313
00:22:36,813 --> 00:22:39,271
Now I'm worried about
what my wife thinks of me.

314
00:22:41,521 --> 00:22:42,938
Now that you mention it,

315
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:47,188
sexual concerns aren't just
a woman's issue.

316
00:22:48,438 --> 00:22:50,896
With so many different kinds of concerns,

317
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:53,063
we need an expert who can talk about them.

318
00:22:53,146 --> 00:22:55,563
Who'd make a good commentator?

319
00:22:57,771 --> 00:22:59,230
How about Furuya?

320
00:22:59,313 --> 00:23:01,146
-Well…
-Furuya, huh?

321
00:23:01,230 --> 00:23:02,480
Is he not a good fit?

322
00:23:02,563 --> 00:23:04,605
<i>He wanted to do it without a condom.</i>

323
00:23:04,688 --> 00:23:08,271
<i>Aren't you worried about things</i>
<i>like pregnancy or STDs?</i>

324
00:23:08,355 --> 00:23:09,271
<i>I totally am.</i>

325
00:23:09,355 --> 00:23:10,438
<i>Right, of course.</i>

326
00:23:10,521 --> 00:23:14,521
<i>My husband and I haven't had sex</i>
<i>for about two years.</i>

327
00:23:14,605 --> 00:23:17,771
<i>So I'm looking for someone on dating apps.</i>

328
00:23:17,855 --> 00:23:19,438
<i>You mean multiple partners?</i>

329
00:23:19,521 --> 00:23:20,355
Okay.

330
00:23:20,438 --> 00:23:21,313
<i>Yes.</i>

331
00:23:21,813 --> 00:23:23,355
Let's take a short break.

332
00:23:23,438 --> 00:23:24,438
Okay.

333
00:23:32,355 --> 00:23:34,813
-Hello.
-Hello.

334
00:23:39,313 --> 00:23:41,105
Are things going well?

335
00:23:41,605 --> 00:23:42,813
Thanks.

336
00:23:42,896 --> 00:23:43,980
No problem.

337
00:23:45,230 --> 00:23:47,730
Well, the footage is looking good.

338
00:23:47,813 --> 00:23:50,230
We're just having trouble
finding a commentator.

339
00:23:50,730 --> 00:23:52,563
I see.

340
00:23:58,396 --> 00:23:59,813
Yumi.

341
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:04,230
Can I ask you something?

342
00:24:05,105 --> 00:24:05,938
What is it?

343
00:24:07,605 --> 00:24:10,563
What's your relationship with Mr. Kazuma?

344
00:24:11,396 --> 00:24:12,396
Huh?

345
00:24:13,355 --> 00:24:14,563
What do you mean?

346
00:24:15,063 --> 00:24:16,688
We're just coworkers.

347
00:24:16,771 --> 00:24:18,521
That's not what I mean.

348
00:24:18,605 --> 00:24:21,521
What do you think of him as a man?

349
00:24:23,313 --> 00:24:24,313
What?

350
00:24:26,271 --> 00:24:28,063
Could it be you like--

351
00:24:28,146 --> 00:24:29,188
I don't.

352
00:24:30,396 --> 00:24:31,521
Not at all.

353
00:24:32,021 --> 00:24:33,521
-I thought so.
-Yeah.

354
00:24:35,563 --> 00:24:38,813
But you've gone out
to eat with him, haven't you?

355
00:24:39,938 --> 00:24:42,855
Only because he's my senior.

356
00:24:45,230 --> 00:24:46,230
Huh?

357
00:24:46,980 --> 00:24:48,105
No way.

358
00:24:48,188 --> 00:24:49,605
Are you telling me…

359
00:24:50,271 --> 00:24:55,313
I think he definitely has a thing for you.

360
00:24:56,730 --> 00:24:57,980
I see.

361
00:24:59,188 --> 00:25:00,938
If that's true…

362
00:25:03,188 --> 00:25:04,188
that's pretty bad.

363
00:25:04,271 --> 00:25:05,813
Yeah, it is.

364
00:25:06,313 --> 00:25:09,188
Who would even do something
like that nowadays?

365
00:25:09,271 --> 00:25:11,688
I mean, use their seniority
to cross the line?

366
00:25:11,771 --> 00:25:13,271
You never know.

367
00:25:13,355 --> 00:25:18,605
Guys like him can be
surprisingly oblivious about that stuff.

368
00:25:18,688 --> 00:25:19,730
I'm glad.

369
00:25:19,813 --> 00:25:23,855
The last thing I wanted was
to have drama on my show.

370
00:25:23,938 --> 00:25:26,271
I was a little worried about you two.

371
00:25:26,355 --> 00:25:28,021
Don't worry. There's no way.

372
00:25:28,105 --> 00:25:29,688
-Right?
-Yeah.

373
00:25:29,771 --> 00:25:30,938
No way.

374
00:25:31,021 --> 00:25:33,896
Honestly, what a relief.

375
00:25:35,438 --> 00:25:37,730
I told you it's a misunderstanding!

376
00:25:40,438 --> 00:25:44,355
She's not saying it was sexual
or academic harassment, is she?

377
00:25:45,521 --> 00:25:46,438
No.

378
00:25:46,938 --> 00:25:48,771
-It's just…
-Look.

379
00:25:49,563 --> 00:25:51,521
If she doesn't want to come,
she can say no.

380
00:25:51,605 --> 00:25:53,646
I'm not forcing her or anything.

381
00:25:57,230 --> 00:26:00,855
As a student, there are benefits
to attending conferences.

382
00:26:01,355 --> 00:26:05,396
And there's a clear power imbalance
between professors and students.

383
00:26:10,146 --> 00:26:12,021
"What if I say no to lunch?"

384
00:26:13,021 --> 00:26:14,771
"What if I return the gift?"

385
00:26:15,688 --> 00:26:18,980
If she's afraid of upsetting you

386
00:26:19,063 --> 00:26:22,063
and can't bring herself to say no,

387
00:26:22,771 --> 00:26:24,313
that's already harassment.

388
00:26:25,896 --> 00:26:28,146
That girl didn't seem that way at all.

389
00:26:28,230 --> 00:26:29,438
Not "that girl."

390
00:26:31,188 --> 00:26:33,188
Her name is Yuka Namioka.

391
00:26:36,271 --> 00:26:40,855
Weren't you ignoring
her wishes and feelings

392
00:26:40,938 --> 00:26:44,813
and putting your own
expectations and assumptions first?

393
00:26:46,896 --> 00:26:48,146
As a result,

394
00:26:48,646 --> 00:26:52,438
wasn't there a part of you
that treated her like a doll?

395
00:26:58,521 --> 00:27:00,438
My father was like that too.

396
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:04,605
He disregarded my mother's feelings

397
00:27:06,896 --> 00:27:09,480
and kept forcing his ideal image onto her.

398
00:27:11,980 --> 00:27:13,396
Because of that,

399
00:27:14,313 --> 00:27:18,813
my mother spent years living in misery.

400
00:27:21,188 --> 00:27:23,646
That's got nothing to do with me.

401
00:27:25,646 --> 00:27:26,646
No.

402
00:27:28,063 --> 00:27:29,730
Back then,

403
00:27:30,230 --> 00:27:32,230
I couldn't do anything for my parents.

404
00:27:34,355 --> 00:27:37,646
But now,

405
00:27:38,146 --> 00:27:41,396
I've come to believe that I might be able
to help someone in need.

406
00:27:48,855 --> 00:27:52,105
If something happens, it'll be too late.

407
00:28:00,605 --> 00:28:02,271
Won't you consider

408
00:28:03,771 --> 00:28:05,438
trying my therapy?

409
00:28:09,855 --> 00:28:11,271
Fine.

410
00:28:11,355 --> 00:28:13,063
I can't say no to you.

411
00:28:17,230 --> 00:28:18,813
Thank you.

412
00:28:43,980 --> 00:28:46,105
Hello, Ichinose?

413
00:28:47,271 --> 00:28:48,271
<i>Yeah.</i>

414
00:28:49,605 --> 00:28:50,605
Um…

415
00:28:53,271 --> 00:28:55,105
Can I talk to you about something?

416
00:29:16,813 --> 00:29:19,438
How has your mother been since then?

417
00:29:20,563 --> 00:29:22,730
She seems to be stable.

418
00:29:25,105 --> 00:29:27,730
But she hasn't regained
consciousness yet.

419
00:29:30,313 --> 00:29:31,355
I see.

420
00:29:52,730 --> 00:29:53,688
Sorry.

421
00:29:54,188 --> 00:29:56,313
I know I said I wanted to talk,

422
00:29:56,396 --> 00:29:59,188
but I don't know what to say.

423
00:30:01,563 --> 00:30:02,646
That's okay.

424
00:30:02,730 --> 00:30:03,813
Take your time.

425
00:30:10,688 --> 00:30:12,480
Whenever you're ready,

426
00:30:12,563 --> 00:30:13,688
I'm here to listen.

427
00:30:39,271 --> 00:30:44,855
I've been working as a sex therapist
as a way to avoid

428
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:46,980
facing things with my parents.

429
00:30:48,771 --> 00:30:50,188
That's the truth.

430
00:30:53,188 --> 00:30:55,271
Professor Toyohara asked me too.

431
00:30:57,938 --> 00:31:02,230
"Was this a path
you actually chose for yourself?"

432
00:31:06,855 --> 00:31:09,188
Even if it was to avoid them,

433
00:31:10,646 --> 00:31:15,021
I'm sure there are many people
who were saved by you.

434
00:31:24,605 --> 00:31:25,646
That's why

435
00:31:27,105 --> 00:31:29,146
I want to choose it again.

436
00:31:32,896 --> 00:31:36,480
I want to choose this job for myself

437
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:39,188
all over again.

438
00:31:42,521 --> 00:31:44,438
Not to look the other way…

439
00:31:47,938 --> 00:31:49,271
but to face things with…

440
00:31:51,896 --> 00:31:53,480
my clients,

441
00:31:54,521 --> 00:31:55,730
my parents…

442
00:32:03,021 --> 00:32:04,521
and myself.

443
00:32:10,396 --> 00:32:12,188
Natsume told me

444
00:32:13,396 --> 00:32:15,313
that "No matter what form they take,

445
00:32:15,813 --> 00:32:20,063
the fragrance of a flower
that once bloomed always lingers."

446
00:32:32,521 --> 00:32:34,730
Can I say something too?

447
00:32:50,563 --> 00:32:51,646
I…

448
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:55,938
want you to be on the show.

449
00:32:58,271 --> 00:32:59,105
Huh?

450
00:33:01,355 --> 00:33:05,688
Sex is difficult to talk about after all.

451
00:33:07,063 --> 00:33:11,230
Many people think
that they can't talk to anyone.

452
00:33:13,313 --> 00:33:14,313
So…

453
00:33:16,271 --> 00:33:18,063
I want them to know

454
00:33:19,230 --> 00:33:23,646
that there are people like you
who'll listen to them sincerely.

455
00:33:30,438 --> 00:33:31,896
Will you be on the show?

456
00:33:39,980 --> 00:33:42,855
How has he been doing since then?

457
00:33:43,730 --> 00:33:46,771
You don't need to go
through me anymore, do you?

458
00:33:46,855 --> 00:33:48,855
He's figured everything out.

459
00:33:50,146 --> 00:33:53,063
He won't open up to me now.

460
00:33:54,855 --> 00:33:59,521
Who was it that dumped him on me
and told me to help him?

461
00:34:00,105 --> 00:34:03,063
You went and made yourself the bad guy.

462
00:34:03,605 --> 00:34:05,271
And you were having fun.

463
00:34:05,355 --> 00:34:06,730
Of course I was.

464
00:34:06,813 --> 00:34:11,188
It was like having a front-row seat
to a dating reality show. I had fun.

465
00:34:12,605 --> 00:34:14,230
<i>CTN special feature.</i>

466
00:34:16,813 --> 00:34:18,105
<i>Tomorrow on Central TV…</i>

467
00:34:18,188 --> 00:34:19,896
Can he move forward?

468
00:34:19,980 --> 00:34:21,438
<i>At 4:45 p.m.</i>

469
00:34:21,521 --> 00:34:23,313
Her presence

470
00:34:24,063 --> 00:34:27,230
has forced him to face his past,
whether he likes it or not.

471
00:34:27,313 --> 00:34:30,896
<i>Sex therapist Dr. Ichito Shimotori</i>
<i>joins us as our guest.</i>

472
00:34:30,980 --> 00:34:34,646
<i>We'll discuss the sexual concerns</i>
<i>people can't tell anyone about.</i>

473
00:34:36,896 --> 00:34:39,313
Yumi really took the plunge.

474
00:34:50,105 --> 00:34:54,105
I had a health checkup recently,
and they found a few issues.

475
00:34:54,188 --> 00:34:55,230
What? Really?

476
00:34:55,313 --> 00:34:57,688
I'm fine, but I thought
I'd be more careful.

477
00:34:57,771 --> 00:34:59,605
-Let's both be careful.
-Yes.

478
00:35:00,105 --> 00:35:01,730
After the break,

479
00:35:01,813 --> 00:35:04,438
our special feature
for "Women Leading the Future" Week.

480
00:35:05,605 --> 00:35:07,021
We're at commercial!

481
00:35:12,646 --> 00:35:14,605
Dr. Shimotori's here.

482
00:35:21,188 --> 00:35:22,313
It's okay.

483
00:35:22,813 --> 00:35:25,021
Whatever happens, I'm here for you.

484
00:35:26,605 --> 00:35:27,855
You're so dependable.

485
00:35:29,271 --> 00:35:30,605
I'm a pro, after all.

486
00:35:34,063 --> 00:35:35,730
-I'll put your mic on.
-Okay.

487
00:35:58,146 --> 00:35:59,730
Five seconds to air!

488
00:36:00,813 --> 00:36:01,938
Three.

489
00:36:02,021 --> 00:36:03,063
Two…

490
00:36:04,313 --> 00:36:07,813
Up next, our "Women Leading
the Future" Week special.

491
00:36:07,896 --> 00:36:10,730
Ms. Ichinose, what is today's topic about?

492
00:36:10,813 --> 00:36:11,730
Yes.

493
00:36:11,813 --> 00:36:13,605
Tonight on Twilight News,

494
00:36:13,688 --> 00:36:16,146
we'll take a look at the sexual concerns

495
00:36:16,230 --> 00:36:19,521
women leading the future
struggle to talk about.

496
00:36:20,271 --> 00:36:22,605
That's quite a bold topic.

497
00:36:22,688 --> 00:36:26,230
Sexual concerns are often seen
as embarrassing

498
00:36:26,313 --> 00:36:29,230
or obscene.

499
00:36:29,313 --> 00:36:33,480
But especially in Japan,
where sex education has lagged behind,

500
00:36:33,563 --> 00:36:36,313
we need an environment
where people can talk

501
00:36:36,396 --> 00:36:39,771
about these issues more openly.

502
00:36:40,771 --> 00:36:42,021
I see.

503
00:36:42,105 --> 00:36:44,105
First, please take a look at this.

504
00:36:44,896 --> 00:36:46,230
<i>Excuse me.</i>

505
00:36:46,313 --> 00:36:47,146
Video's rolling.

506
00:36:48,813 --> 00:36:50,396
-This way, please.
-Okay.

507
00:37:01,771 --> 00:37:03,605
-Take a seat.
-Thank you.

508
00:37:06,146 --> 00:37:07,480
Hello.

509
00:37:13,230 --> 00:37:14,855
All right.

510
00:37:14,938 --> 00:37:17,230
Our star's finally here.

511
00:37:17,313 --> 00:37:19,605
I'm surprised you agreed to this.

512
00:37:19,688 --> 00:37:22,855
We don't get many chances
to pull ratings like this.

513
00:37:22,938 --> 00:37:25,063
I pitched it hard to the higher-ups.

514
00:37:25,146 --> 00:37:26,813
Five seconds to the studio.

515
00:37:28,063 --> 00:37:29,146
Three.

516
00:37:29,230 --> 00:37:30,230
Two…

517
00:37:32,188 --> 00:37:34,146
After doing those interviews,

518
00:37:34,230 --> 00:37:36,938
I realized far more people than I imagined

519
00:37:37,021 --> 00:37:39,355
have sexual concerns
they can't tell anyone about.

520
00:37:39,438 --> 00:37:42,396
Here's a look at some of
the most common responses.

521
00:37:42,896 --> 00:37:46,396
It seems people have
all kinds of concerns.

522
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:47,980
That's right.

523
00:37:48,063 --> 00:37:54,938
Joining us today is psychiatrist
and AASECT-certified sex therapist

524
00:37:55,021 --> 00:37:59,063
Dr. Ichito Shimotori.

525
00:37:59,605 --> 00:38:01,605
Thank you for joining us, Dr. Shimotori.

526
00:38:03,313 --> 00:38:04,938
Thank you for having me.

527
00:38:05,021 --> 00:38:11,146
You've worked with countless patients
at your clinic, haven't you?

528
00:38:11,730 --> 00:38:12,730
Yes.

529
00:38:13,396 --> 00:38:15,521
The term "sex therapy"

530
00:38:15,605 --> 00:38:18,313
isn't very familiar to us.

531
00:38:18,396 --> 00:38:20,521
What kind of treatment do you provide?

532
00:38:21,105 --> 00:38:22,105
Well…

533
00:38:24,855 --> 00:38:26,146
Before I answer that,

534
00:38:26,938 --> 00:38:30,313
I'd like to tell you
a little about myself.

535
00:38:33,855 --> 00:38:37,313
I'm sure many of you
are curious about my past.

536
00:38:47,813 --> 00:38:50,396
As reported by some weekly tabloids,

537
00:38:51,063 --> 00:38:52,521
seventeen years ago,

538
00:38:53,021 --> 00:38:58,938
my father assaulted the man
my mother was having an affair with.

539
00:39:00,980 --> 00:39:02,230
Let him go on.

540
00:39:02,896 --> 00:39:04,063
Let him continue.

541
00:39:05,021 --> 00:39:09,605
It's true that the incident
played a major role in my decision

542
00:39:09,688 --> 00:39:12,146
to become a sex therapist.

543
00:39:13,855 --> 00:39:17,688
Back then, if sex therapy
had been more accessible,

544
00:39:18,646 --> 00:39:20,688
the incident may have been prevented.

545
00:39:22,396 --> 00:39:23,813
<i>My father and mother</i>

546
00:39:24,771 --> 00:39:27,355
<i>might not have ended up the way they did.</i>

547
00:39:28,896 --> 00:39:30,813
You can do it.

548
00:39:32,271 --> 00:39:33,271
<i>Of course,</i>

549
00:39:34,105 --> 00:39:35,896
<i>we can't change the past.</i>

550
00:39:37,230 --> 00:39:41,855
<i>But by treating my clients</i>
<i>with that in mind,</i>

551
00:39:42,688 --> 00:39:44,146
<i>my hope is to help</i>

552
00:39:44,813 --> 00:39:48,938
<i>people like my mother, who use sex</i>
<i>in a way that hurts themselves.</i>

553
00:39:50,855 --> 00:39:51,855
<i>And…</i>

554
00:39:52,563 --> 00:39:57,105
<i>I hope I can help prevent people</i>
<i>from hurting others</i>

555
00:39:57,188 --> 00:39:59,646
<i>like my father did.</i>

556
00:40:06,938 --> 00:40:08,355
Thank you.

557
00:40:10,521 --> 00:40:13,855
Today, we'll focus on some of the concerns

558
00:40:13,938 --> 00:40:16,355
we heard most often.

559
00:40:16,438 --> 00:40:19,521
Dr. Shimotori will help us explore them.

560
00:40:20,146 --> 00:40:21,146
Yes.

561
00:40:21,688 --> 00:40:23,146
Let's start with this.

562
00:40:23,230 --> 00:40:25,980
<i>By talking openly about things</i>
<i>like the need to feel loved,</i>

563
00:40:26,063 --> 00:40:28,105
<i>without blaming each other,</i>

564
00:40:28,188 --> 00:40:32,438
<i>I think couples can deepen</i>
<i>their understanding of one another.</i>

565
00:40:32,521 --> 00:40:33,855
<i>Next…</i>

566
00:40:33,938 --> 00:40:36,188
You're so cool, Doctor!

567
00:40:36,271 --> 00:40:38,521
<i>"I can't tell my partner</i>
<i>to use contraception."</i>

568
00:40:38,605 --> 00:40:41,771
<i>At times, because you're afraid</i>
<i>they'll dislike you,</i>

569
00:40:41,855 --> 00:40:45,188
<i>you end up going along</i>
<i>with what they want.</i>

570
00:40:45,271 --> 00:40:48,063
<i>So, it's best to have a relationship</i>
<i>where you can say no.</i>

571
00:40:48,146 --> 00:40:50,688
<i>There's solo sex and partnered sex.</i>

572
00:40:50,771 --> 00:40:53,146
<i>I recently learned</i>
<i>there's also a virtual option</i>

573
00:40:53,230 --> 00:40:56,938
<i>that falls somewhere in between.</i>

574
00:40:58,271 --> 00:41:01,146
<i>I think it's important</i>
<i>for people to explore</i>

575
00:41:01,230 --> 00:41:03,646
<i>the approach to sexuality</i>
<i>that suits them best.</i>

576
00:41:03,730 --> 00:41:06,271
Here's another concern
many people brought up.

577
00:41:06,355 --> 00:41:11,188
"Is it weird for women to masturbate?"

578
00:41:11,688 --> 00:41:13,730
Regarding this topic,

579
00:41:13,813 --> 00:41:16,271
someone once asked me…

580
00:41:18,521 --> 00:41:21,646
<i>"Why do we call masturbation</i>
<i>'to comfort yourself'?"</i>

581
00:41:22,146 --> 00:41:24,188
<i>"Just like the term 'self-pleasure,'</i>

582
00:41:24,271 --> 00:41:27,063
<i>why not think of it</i>
<i>as pleasuring yourself?"</i>

583
00:41:30,771 --> 00:41:32,938
I also pleasure myself.

584
00:41:35,188 --> 00:41:37,605
I don't think it's weird at all.

585
00:41:38,688 --> 00:41:40,605
I do it pretty often too.

586
00:41:41,855 --> 00:41:44,438
That's not weird, is it, Doctor?

587
00:41:44,521 --> 00:41:46,146
No. Of course not.

588
00:41:46,230 --> 00:41:50,355
For example, I had a client
who masturbated so often

589
00:41:50,438 --> 00:41:52,688
they couldn't focus on work.

590
00:41:53,313 --> 00:41:56,396
<i>The act itself isn't the problem.</i>

591
00:41:56,480 --> 00:41:59,480
He's talking about me!

592
00:41:59,563 --> 00:42:01,188
<i>…how you control it…</i>

593
00:42:01,271 --> 00:42:04,105
Hey! Quit climbing and come watch!
He's talking about me.

594
00:42:04,188 --> 00:42:06,813
So far, we've explored

595
00:42:07,313 --> 00:42:09,896
sexual concerns
people can't tell anyone about

596
00:42:09,980 --> 00:42:12,313
from female perspectives.

597
00:42:12,896 --> 00:42:14,313
<i>But Doctor--</i>

598
00:42:14,396 --> 00:42:15,730
We're the number-one trend!

599
00:42:16,730 --> 00:42:17,688
We're the top trend!

600
00:42:17,771 --> 00:42:20,105
Be quiet! This is the important part.

601
00:42:20,188 --> 00:42:22,230
<i>This may sound simple,</i>

602
00:42:22,313 --> 00:42:24,480
but listening to your partner

603
00:42:24,563 --> 00:42:27,938
and making an effort
to be honest about how you feel

604
00:42:29,730 --> 00:42:31,188
is the only way I believe

605
00:42:31,271 --> 00:42:34,313
we can bridge gaps
and clear up misunderstandings.

606
00:42:34,396 --> 00:42:35,855
That's true.

607
00:42:36,355 --> 00:42:39,688
You'll never know what someone
really thinks of you

608
00:42:39,771 --> 00:42:42,521
unless you ask them.

609
00:42:42,605 --> 00:42:43,605
Yes.

610
00:42:44,271 --> 00:42:48,438
I've learned that firsthand
myself recently.

611
00:42:48,521 --> 00:42:50,480
Did something happen, Mr. Kazuma?

612
00:42:51,771 --> 00:42:52,688
No…

613
00:42:53,188 --> 00:42:54,188
Not really.

614
00:42:58,105 --> 00:42:59,396
Doctor,

615
00:42:59,480 --> 00:43:01,563
do you have a final message
for our viewers?

616
00:43:02,605 --> 00:43:03,605
Yes.

617
00:43:07,646 --> 00:43:11,146
For people living in the modern world,

618
00:43:11,230 --> 00:43:14,063
sex is not just about reproduction.

619
00:43:15,480 --> 00:43:19,771
As the meaning and purpose of sex
have become more diverse,

620
00:43:19,855 --> 00:43:23,355
people's concerns
have also grown more complex.

621
00:43:24,855 --> 00:43:28,688
Because each person's concerns
are different,

622
00:43:29,271 --> 00:43:30,855
<i>they feel they can't tell anyone</i>

623
00:43:31,521 --> 00:43:34,396
<i>and end up backing themselves</i>
<i>into a corner.</i>

624
00:43:37,355 --> 00:43:38,730
<i>Before that happens,</i>

625
00:43:39,230 --> 00:43:41,730
<i>I believe there is something I can do.</i>

626
00:43:44,063 --> 00:43:45,063
At this moment,

627
00:43:45,813 --> 00:43:50,396
to anyone struggling with sexual concerns

628
00:43:52,271 --> 00:43:54,438
that they can't tell anyone about…

629
00:44:04,855 --> 00:44:06,105
Don't worry.

630
00:44:07,188 --> 00:44:09,521
Everyone has concerns

631
00:44:10,313 --> 00:44:11,563
when it comes to sex.

632
00:44:20,563 --> 00:44:23,188
KAWAWA SHRINE

633
00:44:23,271 --> 00:44:30,271
LANTERN FESTIVAL

634
00:44:40,021 --> 00:44:41,313
There we go.

635
00:44:42,271 --> 00:44:43,688
Wow!

636
00:44:43,771 --> 00:44:44,605
Wow.

637
00:44:44,688 --> 00:44:45,771
It's beautiful.

638
00:44:45,855 --> 00:44:47,938
-This is amazing.
-Yeah.

639
00:44:55,730 --> 00:44:57,646
It's so magical.

640
00:45:06,313 --> 00:45:08,355
I feel like it's finally started moving.

641
00:45:09,646 --> 00:45:10,855
What has?

642
00:45:13,146 --> 00:45:16,771
The clock that stopped 17 years ago.

643
00:45:23,980 --> 00:45:25,063
You're right.

644
00:45:29,813 --> 00:45:31,021
Thank you

645
00:45:31,646 --> 00:45:34,480
for listening to me.

646
00:45:37,021 --> 00:45:38,646
I should be thanking you.

647
00:45:40,896 --> 00:45:42,896
For listening to me.

648
00:47:28,980 --> 00:47:35,980
S&amp;X

649
00:49:43,480 --> 00:49:45,396
Subtitle translation by: Yuki Asami

